---
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { join } from "node:path";
import Doc from "../../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const upstreamLicense = readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), "LICENSES", "models.dev-MIT.txt"), "utf8");
const piLicense = readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), "LICENSES", "pi-MIT.txt"), "utf8");
const ownLicense = readFileSync(join(process.cwd(), "LICENSE"), "utf8");
---

<Doc
  title="Licensing and attribution"
  description="Licences and attribution for the providers.dev dataset, the models.dev data it builds on and pi's catalog shown beside it."
  lead="The baseline of this catalog is imported from models.dev, and the model catalog of pi is imported beside it; both are published under the MIT License. providers.dev is an independent project and is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by models.dev, pi or any listed provider."
  toc={[
    { id: "attribution", label: "Attribution" },
    { id: "use", label: "Using the data" },
    { id: "upstream", label: "models.dev licence" },
    { id: "pi", label: "pi licence" },
    { id: "own", label: "providers.dev licence" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="attribution">Attribution</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every provider and entry whose <code>providers_dev.origin</code> is <code>upstream</code> comes from <a href="https://models.dev">models.dev</a> (<a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev">source</a>), except the fields listed in its <code>providers_dev.provenance</code>.</li>
      <li>Every <code>providers_dev.pi</code> block of an entry comes from the model catalog of <a href="https://pi.dev/models">pi</a> (<a href="https://github.com/earendil-works/pi">source</a>), imported from <a href="https://pi.dev/api/models"><code>pi.dev/api/models</code></a>.</li>
      <li>Everything else under a <code>providers_dev</code> key, every entry whose origin is <code>added</code>, and every field listed in a <code>provenance</code> array is by providers.dev.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This marking is kept through every export, so a consumer of <code>/api.json</code> can always tell the two apart.</p>

    <h2 id="use">Using the data</h2>
    <p>
      providers.dev additions, corrections and code are under the MIT License below. When redistributing the dataset, keep every notice. They ship with the dataset as{" "}
      <a href="/data/LICENSE-models.dev.txt"><code>/data/LICENSE-models.dev.txt</code></a>, <a href="/data/LICENSE-pi.txt"><code>/data/LICENSE-pi.txt</code></a> and{" "}
      <a href="/data/NOTICE.txt"><code>/data/NOTICE.txt</code></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Model and provider names are trademarks of their owners and are used only to identify them. The data is provided as is; confirm a limit against the provider's own documentation before
      relying on it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="upstream">models.dev licence</h2>
    <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap">{upstreamLicense}</pre>

    <h2 id="pi">pi licence</h2>
    <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap">{piLicense}</pre>

    <h2 id="own">providers.dev licence</h2>
    <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap">{ownLicense}</pre>
  </div>
</Doc>
